Attribution
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Portions of this project are informed by, and in places adapted from, G-Engine
by Clark Kromenaker (https://github.com/kromenak/gengine), licensed under the
GNU General Public License version 3. G-Engine is used as the behavioral oracle
and file-format reference for GK3Reborn. Files that adapt G-Engine code carry a
per-file attribution notice.

The fingerprint table in src/GK3Reborn.Engine/Game/FingerprintKit.cs — which prints are on
which surface, and what lifting each one gives and scores — is adapted from G-Engine's
FingerprintScreen.cpp, and carries the attribution in its own header comment.

Three of G-Engine's own data files are adapted here, in src/GK3Reborn.Engine/Assets/Story:

  Pockets.txt     what Gabriel and Grace are carrying when the game begins
  Scores.txt      what each of the game's score events is worth
  Timeblocks.shp  the rules that decide when a point in the story is over

None is in the game's own data. The original compiled all three into its executable,
so a reimplementation has to restore them; G-Engine reconstructed them, and these
are adapted from that work under the same licence. Each carries the attribution in
its own header.

File-format understanding also draws on GK3 Tools
(https://sourceforge.net/projects/gk3tools/).

