Third-party components
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Redistributed third-party components and their licenses are listed in
licenses/THIRD-PARTY.md, which travels in every published archive.

The interface's typeface is Noto Serif Regular (version 1.07), Copyright 2012
Google Inc., licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1. It is
carried inside GK3Reborn.Engine as an embedded resource at
src/GK3Reborn.Engine/Assets/Fonts/NotoSerif-Regular.ttf, and its licence is
included in that file's own name table. The OFL permits this redistribution;
the font is not sold on its own and its name is not used to promote anything.
See https://scripts.sil.org/OFL. A .ttf or .otf placed in the content
workspace's enhanced/fonts directory is used in preference to it, which is how
the typeface is changed without rebuilding.

None of GK3's own fonts are redistributed. They are read from the player's
installation like every other original asset, and are still what the interface
falls back to when no outline font can be read.

FFmpeg decodes the cutscenes, through FFMediaToolkit (MIT) over FFmpeg's own
shared libraries. It is not part of this source tree - the libraries are found
at run time in libs/<rid> or on the system, and a machine with no FFmpeg runs
the game without its cutscenes - but the binary releases published from this
repository do carry it, so its terms travel with them.

What they carry is an unmodified LGPL shared build of FFmpeg 7.1, licensed
under the GNU Lesser General Public License version 2.1 or later. Nothing is
statically linked and nothing has been altered: the libraries are loaded at run
time, and any other build of the same generation - avcodec 61, avformat 61,
avutil 59, swscale 8, swresample 5 - can replace them by being dropped in.
build/fetch-native.sh records the exact upstream release these are taken from
and the SHA-256 of each archive. The corresponding source is FFmpeg itself at
tag n7.1, https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg, and the recipe that produced the
binaries is https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds - both offering the same
access as the release the binaries themselves come from.

MoltenVK travels in the macOS bundle, as libs/osx-arm64/libMoltenVK.dylib. It
is Vulkan over Metal and it is the only Vulkan an Apple silicon Mac has, so a
bundle without it renders nothing at all. Version 1.4.2, unmodified, Copyright
2015 The Brenwill Workshop Ltd., licensed under the Apache License 2.0. See
https://github.com/KhronosGroup/MoltenVK.
